# <span style="color: #e6a050">Better Spells</span>

</div>

<div style="text-align: center">

<span style="color: #e6a050">*Tune every spell to your liking: longer, stronger, wider, cheaper, faster, more summons.*</span>  
*<span style="color: #e6a050">Or nerf them. All while you play.</span>*

</div>

<div style="text-align: center">

The source code for all my Enshrouded mods is available on [GitHub](https://github.com/Fuzen777/Enshrouded-Mods) (MIT)

</div>

---

Better Spells is a **Kiln** mod that gives every spell in Enshrouded its own settings : mana cost, cast time, damage, duration, radius, summon health, summons per cast and more. 

Press **Shift+F3** in game, click a spell, and change it. Every change applies right away to what you cast next, with no restart.

Every setting starts at the game's own value, so nothing changes until you decide it should. Multipliers go both ways : buff the spells you love, or make the game harder.

---

## Features

### Setting Windows

- Opens with **Shift+F3** (or the button on the mod's page in Kiln's menu), where you left it, at the same size.
- With **Grimoire** installed, the settings window and the grimoire open side by side, even on the same key, and move together while they touch. Hold **Shift** while dragging to move one alone.
- Spells are laid out as **icon rows by element** : Fire, Ice, Lightning, Shroud, Summons, Others, and Items. Click a spell's icon to open its card.
- Each setting is a simple **− value +** control. The mouse wheel works over any value; hold **Shift** for 10 steps, **Ctrl** for 100.
- A **dot** marks every spell you have changed, so you can see your edits at a glance.
- Every setting has its explanation on hover.

### Settings for Every Spell

- **Mana Cost** (x0.1 to x10), on every spell.
- **Cast Time** (x0.1 to x10): how soon the spell is ready again.
- **Damage** (x0.1 to x50): multiplies the spell's own share of the damage.
- **Duration** (x0.1 to x10), for every spell that lasts: Fire Pillar, Blizzard, Ball Lightning, Acid Cone, Root, Magic Shield, Totems, Skeletons and Lightning Wisps. The tooltip follows.
- **Radius** (x0.1 to x5) for Fireball, Fire Pillar, Light Burst, Ice Bolt, Blizzard, Ball Lightning, Shroud Meteor and Root. Areas, visuals and tooltips follow.
- **Health** (x0.1 to x10) for Totems, Skeletons, Magic Shield and summoning items.

### Global Settings

- Mana Cost, Cast Time, Damage, Duration, Radius and Health for **every spell together**.
- Two modes: **Multiply** (General x2 and Fireball x3 give x6) or **At Least** (General x2 lifts every spell below x2 and leaves Fireball at x3; for Mana Cost and Cast Time, lower wins).

### Summons

- **Per Cast** (1 to 5): Totems, Skeletons and Lightning Wisps place several at once for one cast's mana.
- **Max Totems / Max Skeletons** (1 to 10): how many can be out at once, before skills add to it.
- **Totem Spread**: how far apart the totems of one cast land.
- **Invulnerable Totems**: totems take no damage, like Lightning Wisps.
- **Enemies Ignore Totems** (experimental): enemies stop targeting totems, so they no longer act as decoys.
- **Keep Older Wisps** (experimental): a new Lightning Wisp cast no longer removes your earlier wisps, so they add up while they last.

### Lightning

- **Chain Lightning**: Radius (how far the chain jumps, up to x10) and Lock-On Range (up to x2, the most the game allows).
- **Ball Lightning**: Speed and Hit Rate, besides Duration, Damage and Radius.

### Items that act like spells

- **Skull Vessel**: Mana Cost, Cast Time, Duration, Damage, Health, and **Per Use** (throw up to 5 vessels for one).
- **Fire Wisp Scroll**: Mana Cost, Duration, Damage, Health, and Per Use (up to 5 wisps).
- **Meteor Shower Scroll**: Mana Cost and Damage.
- **Crawler Bomb**: Mana Cost, Cast Time, Duration, Damage and Health.
- The General card covers these too.

### Live, safe and reversible

- Every change applies **while you play**, to what you cast afterwards. No restart, no world reload (except Max Totems and Max Skeletons, which apply when you next load a world).
- Set a value back to x1 and that spell is vanilla again.
- Spells are found by name, not by a fixed list, so all tiers of a spell follow the same setting.

---

## How to Use

1. Load a world and press **Shift+F3**.
2. Click a spell's icon in its element row (or the **General** row to change all spells at once).
3. Use **−** and **+**, or scroll the mouse wheel over a value. Hold **Shift** for 10 steps or **Ctrl** for 100.
4. Cast the spell. The new values apply from that cast on. A totem or skeleton already out keeps its old values until you cast again.
5. Press **Shift+F3** again or **Esc** to close the window. Your settings are saved automatically.

### Tips

- Raising Per Cast? Raise that spell's Mana Cost too if you want to keep it fair (5 wisps for x5 cost).
- On the General card, **At Least** is the easy way to set a floor ("every spell at least x2 damage") without stacking on top of your per-spell values.
- Values below x1 make a spell weaker: handy for a challenge run.

**Changing the key**: it is **Open Settings Window** in the Keys tab of Kiln's menu. The settings themselves are in Kiln's profile (`%LOCALAPPDATA%\Kiln\profiles\<your profile>\config\better-spells.json`), so updating the mod never resets them.

---

## Requirements

- [Kiln](https://github.com/frostdev-ops/kiln) mod loader, **0.2.0-dev.31 or newer**.

## Installation

1. Close the game.
2. Drop the archive on Kiln.
3. Start the game and load a world.
4. Press Shift+F3.

## Compatibility

- Made and tested in single player and worlds you host. Not tested on dedicated servers.
- Other mods that change the same spell values will stack with or overwrite these.

## Known limitations

- Shroud Meteor's ground cursor keeps its size when you raise its Radius (the impact area does grow). Growing it increased the terrain destruction area, which led to temporary freezes. Fun, but not something you’d actually want to deal with.
- Damage multiplies the spell's share only, not your staff's.
- Chain Lightning's Lock-On Range is capped by the game at about x1.75, so the setting stops at x2.
- Skeleton Health scales the skeletons' level-based health, which may not be exactly proportional.
- Ice Totem's chill on enemies keeps its normal length when you raise Totem Duration.
- Heal spells aren’t covered yet… Might do them later.

